  m_text: "The criminal anthropology museum hosts his laboratory collections, research
    materials, and personal archives, allowing visitors to explore the origins of
    modern criminology while critically examining the assumptions and biases that
    guided 19th-century scientific thought. Through this historical lens, the museum
    invites reflection on how ideas about crime, identity, and society have evolved\u2014and
    how they continue to shape contemporary debates."
